>>
Rule 1 (input and values must have the same dtype to avoid dtype-mismatch error)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 2 (values must be scalar or have the same shape as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_2) = 0) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
>>
Rule 3 (out tensor, if provided, must match input’s dtype and shape when values is scalar or shape-equal)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_2) = 0 ∨ (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))) then (dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i))
>>
Rule 4 (real-valued dtypes only: integers or floats; exclude bool and complex)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∧ (1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8)
